you  imagine this shifting gears and moving  out of your house to live in a van  believe it or not this is becoming a new  trend with more people adopting a  freewheeling lifestyle I decided to try  it out in California's high desert where  I met a man named Bob Wells he's a  former grocery store clerk who's become  a guru of life on the road what do you  do  hundred miles from nowhere car breaks  down you're in your home you pull over  and you make dinner I think the average  person might come in to a van like this  and think it's a little cramped I think  anybody in the right mind would say this  is a little crap I sleep in here and I  live out there you have enough money at  this point you could go live in a home I  could live at home but why would I  torture myself  [Laughter]  this beauty is our minivan where we have  spent the past two nights it is a  perfect balance between comfort and  freedom bob says and so I can give you  the tour we sleep here that's the  bedroom we put our toiletries here  that's in effect the bathroom you can  see some notebooks up front that's the  office we've got food in the tents over  here and the best part the backyard okay  you can watch my entire journey the van  live this weekend on CBS Sunday morning  I learned a lot and the the biggest  thing is pay your rent

